<VI _name="lvai_icon_get_vi_icons_n_file.vi" description="Batch read-back of VI icons to PNGs in ONE LabVIEW call, without changing the VIs. vi list and png list are the paths of two text files holding absolute paths, each entry followed by a semicolon, paired by position - files because the runner cannot set an array and a long string input passes the answer size limit from about 100 paths. Per pair - Open VI Reference, Save VI Icon to File, Close Reference - one line of error code TAB png path into report, and ok count = entries with code 0. The output folders must exist and every PNG path must stay under MAX_PATH - otherwise NOTHING is written and the code is still 0, so count the files. Run with the project CLOSED. Measured in a pilot project on LabVIEW 2026 Q3 with labview-mcp 1.8.5 (146 VIs in one call).">
